          "message": "Bolt: add execute_cypher string-in workload benchmark (no fix) (#3832)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds `examples/bolt_cypher_workload.rs`, a deterministic,\npublic-API-driven benchmark for `AletheiaDB::execute_cypher`'s full\nstring-in path (lex, parse, plan, execute). No existing benchmark\nexercises this: `benches/` has no `cypher` entry, and `execute_cypher`\nre-parses its input on every call with no prepared-statement cache —\nexactly the shape an LLM caller or the MCP `query` tool uses, re-issuing\nthe same or similar statement text repeatedly.\n- **No `src/` changes.** This PR ships a benchmark harness only — no\nperformance fix.\n\n## Why no fix\n\nThe workload's query (`WHERE` filtering the pattern's start variable\nwhile `RETURN`ing the end variable) routes through the\nmulti-variable-pattern evaluator (`src/cypher/multi_pattern.rs`).\nProfiling under `valgrind --tool=callgrind` found that evaluator's\nwhole-graph node materialization (`db.current.all_nodes().collect()` + a\nfull `HashMap<NodeId, usize>` index, rebuilt on every call regardless of\nlabel selectivity) contributing a real, identifiable inefficiency — a\nscan/clone that could instead go through the existing borrowed\n`iter_nodes()` / per-id `get_node()` primitives.\n\nI implemented that change and measured it on the same harness:\ninstructions -1.73%, allocation count -0.08%, allocation bytes -3.47% —\nall below this process's impact floor (≥5% / ≥10% / ≥10%).\n`Node`/`PropertyMap` clone turned out to be cheaper than expected, and\nreplacing a pre-built local index with a live `DashMap::get` inside the\ntraversal's inner loop partially offset the savings. Reverted per\nprocess; not shipped.\n\nFull writeup — profile breakdown, the diff tried, the measured\nbefore/after table, and a note on the larger (already-tracked)\n`TODO(perf #549-followup)` binding-clone limitation that's probably the\nreal win in this evaluator — is in #3831.\n\n## What this PR is for\n\nLanding the harness now means the profile and the negative result above\nare reproducible by anyone who checks out this branch, without redoing\nthe setup, and gives a starting point for whoever picks up the larger\nbinding-clone follow-up.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `cargo build --profile bench --features cypher --example\nbolt_cypher_workload` succeeds\n- [x] Native run produces a deterministic `sink=...` line, unchanged\nacross the (reverted) fix attempt\n- [x] `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — clean\n- [x] `cargo clippy --example bolt_cypher_workload --features cypher\n--all-features -- -D warnings` — clean, no warnings\n- [x] `cargo test --lib --features cypher cypher::` — 538 passed, 0\nfailed\n- Reproduce the profile:\n  ```\ncargo build --profile bench --features cypher --example\nbolt_cypher_workload\n  BOLT_NODES=300 BOLT_OUT_DEGREE=6 BOLT_QUERY_ITERS=200 \\\n    valgrind --tool=callgrind --callgrind-out-file=/tmp/cg.out -- \\\n    target/release/examples/bolt_cypher_workload\n  callgrind_annotate --threshold=99.5 /tmp/cg.out | less\n  ```\n\nCloses/references: #3831\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01A1DMzsxvhGVLsj5XEGEmfo\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01A1DMzsxvhGVLsj5XEGEmfo)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
